{
  "dom_id": "step-q73818",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "$\\frac{9{x}^{4}+12{x}^{3}-25}{3x-5}=$",
  "worked_solution": "We can calculate $\\frac{9{x}^{4}+12{x}^{3}-25}{3x-5}$ using synthetic division.\n\nFor synthetic division to work, we need the coefficient of $x$ in the denominator to be equal to $1.$ So first, we factor the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9{x}^{4}+12{x}^{3}-25}{3x-5} & =\\frac{9{x}^{4}+12{x}^{3}-25}{3(x-\\frac{5}{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{9{x}^{4}+12{x}^{3}-25}{(x-\\frac{5}{3})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCarrying out the synthetic division process on $\\frac{9{x}^{4}+12{x}^{3}-25}{(x-\\frac{5}{3})}$, we arrive at the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{4} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ \\frac{5}{3} & 9 & 12 & 0 & 0 & -25 \\\\  & ↓ & 15 & 45 & 75 & 125 \\\\  & 9 & 27 & 45 & 75 & 100\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{9{x}^{4}+12{x}^{3}-25}{(x-\\frac{5}{3})} & =\\frac{1}{3}(9{x}^{3}+27{x}^{2}+45x+75+\\frac{100}{(x-\\frac{5}{3})}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}+9{x}^{2}+15x+25+\\frac{100}{3x-5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our final result is\n\n$$\n\\frac{9{x}^{4}+12{x}^{3}-25}{3x-5}=3{x}^{3}+9{x}^{2}+15x+25+\\frac{100}{3x-5}.\n$$",
